{"contract_id": "ROOT-L13-1292-INVENTORY-COUNT-AGGREGATION", "canonical_owner": "Whole item count across public native inventory stacks", "first_failed_contract_or_unresolved_question": "personal_item_quantity and party_item_quantity sum u32 stack quantities into u32 and feed ammo readiness, tent shelter and material ownership. Establish aggregate bound/uniqueness and carried-versus-owned whole-item semantics; arbitrary many MAX stacks is not an admitted witness.", "source_originals": [1292], "remaining_evidence": ["Native inventory stack admission/merge/count limits, tent custody/rest material consumption, ammunition readiness and all callers/current/aliases."], "dependencies": ["Exact source1292; existing departure alignment, projected fatigue and missing-observation questions; native/current/exact aliases independent."], "closure_condition": "Qualify actual supported producer, API, state, consumer and native behavior with exact current and alias reconciliation; record supported finding/policy/rejection without hypothetical invalid raw-value witnesses.", "later_repair_acceptance_requirements": ["Supported whole counts remain exact across multiple stacks without overflow or wrong shelter/readiness selection.", "Preserve intentional fractional mass versus whole item count distinction and native custody invariants."], "kind": "connected-contract-question", "lens": 13, "exact_source_identities_and_assessed_ranges": [{"source": {"original": 1292, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-strategic-sim/src/live_core/survival.rs", "sha256": "9b69053053efb67e000a8aeafdaf2b7a89678136f4459cf592a6e7e9f391e1ad", "actual_eof": 2550, "object_path": "target/726-audit-adler-20261027/adler-continuation-20261030/objects/9b69053053efb67e000a8aeafdaf2b7a89678136f4459cf592a6e7e9f391e1ad", "source_revision": "6533e444fa37552927070cc8d8190907fd3b413e", "prospective_ranges": [[1, 2550]], "purpose": "Full Lens13 survival supply/recovery/forecast numerical contracts and failure/security acceptance tests; source inspection only, no test execution."}, "registration": {"path": "adler-continuation-20261030/REGISTRATION-ROOT-L13-1292-1293-001.json", "sha256": "019cce7b6837268efaffda48377c65818390fd2d824511f45a3827c8d2d086d0"}, "registration_pointer": "/sources/0", "assessed_ranges": [[1, 2550]], "author": "/root", "untruncated_body_outputs": true, "observations": ["1..29: bounded_grams maps nonfinite/nonpositive kg to0, otherwise rounds kg*1000 and caps at u64 float representation; this is telemetry, not mass admission. Encumbrance remaining uses canonical multiplier, clamp0..1 and canonical basis-point scale. Equipment-ready requires Ready status, bounded wetness and absolute strain (unsigned_abs handles i32 minimum), ammunition floor for ranged, and remaining-bps floor. Exact native bounds and policy constants/rounding require connected ownership.", "32..78: Living IDs are filtered through existing alive character rows and sorted; no dedup here, native membership uniqueness needed. Personal and party item quantities sum raw u32 stacks, not fractional/measured quantities or carried-only custody. Actual native aggregate bound and intended use for whole arrows/tents versus first-aid remains open; no overflow state asserted admitted.", "80..157: Location/custody and row association compare exact typed variants. Carried object root walk rejects cycles/missing/wrong-custody and is bounded MAX_CONTAINER_DEPTH inclusive; row must map exactly one inventory object. No zero ID sentinel or multiple-object acceptance.", "159..235: Stack mass reads scope-specific remaining fraction and calls public_effective_inventory_quantity; missing definition contributes0. Personal carried food uses exact lot.mass_kg.max0, otherwise measured stack mass; water u64 ml casts f32 and converts /1000 to kg. Body mass deliberately excluded. Invalid custody produces infinity, later telemetry maps it0; classification requires supported ID/native provenance, not an arbitrary invalid character.", "237..323: Capacity requires attributes/limbs, else0; missing condition multiplier0, Ready1/Staggered0.5/Incapacitated0. Leg strength weighted by clamped limb health and averaged0.5 then canonical capacity. Party sums living personal loads, carried party food/measured inventory, carried water, and capacities. Exact agreement with authoritative equipment/condition policy still needed; no movement penalty added here.", "325..413: Survival observation requires character, condition and capability (OptionNone on missing); it retains public thermal/wetness/strain, quantities/load/capacity and readiness. Telemetry sums party load, rounds grams, initializes min-encumbrance on first observation and uses saturating count, then records max wetness/abs strain for available living condition rows. Default substitution happens at previously read consumers, not in this Option API.", "415..598: General-store quote requires alive co-located actor, market/generalstore, a unique publicly present provider and visible buy_bps; canonical merchant price with base fallback1, language-adjusted price at0 explicitly upper-bound, then local-problem adjustment. Missing clock makes providerNone. Equipment offer preserves exact(service,provider,quote) after storefront/stock admission. Actual price bound and native quote equivalence remain pending.", "600..651: Stake withdrawal needed0 returns success; requires stake>=needed and summed treasury>=needed; stacks deterministic item/ID order. min(remaining,u32 stack quantity) bounds narrowing to u32 before native withdrawal. Metric increments needed after all calls. Actual native debit/stack/subscription progress invariants remain needed, not the separate temporary-companion settlement helper.", "653..782: Tent missing/provider unavailable explicitly permits bivouac with provenance; missing quote when provider exists defers. Existing party tent quantity>0 is accepted; hypothetical added tent mass is checked before purchase. Payers rank affordability, spendable partycoin+purse-reserve then ID; quantity1 party purchase verifies resulting tent count and records observed coin decrease. This is explicit shelter policy, not a default successful purchase.", "784..940: Missing ranged capability skips ammunition purchase, but final survival observation requires capability and defers absent projection. Arrows purchase only guarded floor-minus-current count, checked hypothetical load, saturating unitquote*missing, own stake withdrawal and postwithdrawal purse reserve; final count>=floor verified. Final readiness first checks partyload, then each living member; empty roster behavior depends on canonical zero-capacity multiplier/caller, not proven safe or invalid here.", "942..1129: Insulation requires exact owned equipped item and placement; deduplicates protected regions before repeating layer contribution; canonical insulation owner. Route origin requires exclusive settlement/case-site, validates degree/E7 points and matching geographic mode, uses explicit zero elevation matching claimed route authority. Start is max available living clocks; no clocks defers; configured start must not precede observed max nor exceed one day. Per-member attributes/limbs/stats/schedule required. Fatigue capacity=(endurance*chest_health).max0.01*1000, camp schedule copies only applicable four allocations. Native units/status/clock completeness need qualification.", "1130..1351: Generated candidate actions filtered exact owner/case, selected Travel state and correct case-site; empty actions denotes direct contract with actionduration0. Positive candidate_wait replaces every forecast calories_used with0 and starting thermal state with default; immediate uses observed wetness/strain and frostbite progress0. Outbound rejects truncation/length mismatch before indexing. Return calories include strenuous max actionduration, then forecasts return. Checks total nonfatigue+projected fatigue, actor Ready at arrival, all-member survivability/thermal; no separate hidden fatigue pool.", "1352..1653: Optional case-site recovery computes common clear duration, accepts1..day, uses canonical camp_fatigue_after and reforecasts return. Recovery thermal branch uses observed wetness/strain with frostbite0 even for delayed candidate, unlike direct action branch default start. Counters saturate; unavailable/complete/fatigue/site mismatch remain distinct; diagnostic action count caps32 only. Selected waiting plan can exceedday search horizon but returned wait=min(planwait,day) with explicit WaitTowardSafePublicRouteWindow; exact continuation revalidation and actual future recovery remain required.", "1654..1970: Direct-route immediate and delayed forecasts reject truncation/cardinality, delayed next-walking wait is rechecked is_walking_time after representable minimum. Unlike generated delayed reset, this branch carries original fatigue and thermal starting state into delayed forecast. Per-member return/action readiness and thermal projections combine; projectionNone conservative false/defer. ReadyWithItinerary retains walking/mode, no elapsed work performed by forecast.", "1972..2115: Field thermal check for active journey uses authoritative camp interval remaining>=request; site mode rejects empty living roster, requires each personal clock/condition/insulation and projected field safety. Site synchronization targets max living clock but then requires each clock/condition/insulation, rejects public critical illness, and predicts each lagging exposure; missing illness is no critical match. Frostbite progress initializes0. No actual rest or synchronization executed by these predicates.", "2117..2449: On-site return decision requires exact current site, origin and geography, max clock and complete per-member recovery inputs. Evaluates return-now, action+return and bounded common recovery+action+return; carries thermal projection state from recovery into action/return, uses canonical camp fatigue, excludes critical illness for action paths. Single-member forecast index0 is intentional; length safeguards delegated to forecast/projection bodies. No private tactical state persisted.", "2451..2550: Departure preparation requires settlement, tent policy, upgrades, ammunition and final readiness, then emits route projection pending exact site. Camp rest requires public party, selects Tent solely if party whole quantity>0 elseBivouac, calls authoritative reducer once and records shelter counts after accepted result. No local duration admission or elapsed success measurement in wrapper; caller/native interval constraints remain independent. No source helper or tests executed."]}], "body_receipt": {"path": "segovb/READ-L13-PARALLEL-328.json", "sha256": "4c295a59d8c3331b0acdeb043d6064b41109c92c5d82b9a5bdf142712d649cca"}, "connected_source_evidence": [], "prior_same_lens_reuses": [], "body_or_population_credit": 0, "new_unique_finding_claimed": false, "current_reconciled": false, "audit_discovery_closed": false}

